    D5  WHAT THE SURVIVING KERNEL IS.  In the deep-MOND limit Delta(x) -> sqrt(x), so
        s * a_0 Delta(g/a_0) = sqrt(s^2 a_0 g) = a_0' Delta(g/a_0') with a_0' = s^2 a_0 EXACTLY:
          verified numerically in the strict deep limit (g << s^2 a_0): max |s*kern(a_0)/kern(s^2 a_0)
          - 1| = 1.3e-02 at s = 0.2, 0.3, 0.438. At the ACTUAL SPARC deep-MOND points the
          degeneracy is only APPROXIMATE, median |ratio - 1| = 0.29-1.32, because
          the interpolation is not yet asymptotic there. So this is an exact statement about the DEEP
          LIMIT and a rough one on the data, and both are reported rather than the flattering one.
        So the surviving kernel term, taken on its own, produces its MOND transition at a_0' = s^2 a_0 <= 0.192 a_0
        = 1.80e-11 m/s^2 -- a factor 5.2 BELOW the acceleration at which the observed RAR turns over.
        For that term to still account for the observed turnover the action's a_0 would have to be 5.2x larger,
        i.e. kappa = 2.60 instead of the fitted 0.4998 -- outside every principle-shaped candidate the
        coefficient programme carries. What actually happens instead is D7: at f = 1 the BTFR zero point is the
        HALO's, so the framework's a_0 is no longer MEASURED by galaxy dynamics at all, and kappa loses the
        empirical anchor (0.465 +/- 0.076 from the BTFR) from which it is quoted.
  [FAIL] D5 the kernel that survives at f = 1 is still the deposited theory's kernel, i.e. it carries the same a_0 and the a_0-Lambda tie still refers to something that acts   (it is not. A partial suppression is EXACTLY degenerate with a smaller a_0 in the strict deep-MOND limit (verified to 1e-02) and roughly so on the data (29%-132% at the actual SPARC deep-MOND points, which are not yet asymptotic), so the surviving kernel has a MOND transition at a_0' = s^2 a_0 <= 0.192 a_0, a factor 5.2 below where the observed RAR turns over -- so the surviving term no longer sets the scale it was built to set. Making it do so would need kappa = 2.60 rather than the fitted 0.4998. The operative consequence is D7's: at f = 1 the BTFR zero point is the HALO's, so the framework's a_0 is not measured by galaxy dynamics any more and kappa loses the 0.465 +/- 0.076 BTFR anchor it is quoted from. Since kappa is FITTED rather than derived this is not a falsification -- it is the loss of the coincidence that motivated the tie)

