==========================================================================================================================
PART E -- THE PRICE.
==========================================================================================================================

    E1  EQUIVALENCE PRINCIPLE.  A kernel whose STRENGTH depends on species composition violates the WEP
        in the gravitational sector twice over, where L50's baryon sourcing violated it once:
          (a) baryons feel the kernel and the cold component does not -- L50's violation, inherited;
          (b) NEW HERE: the force on a BARYON depends on how much OTHER-species matter is nearby. Two
              identical baryonic configurations with the same g_bar accelerate differently according
              to the local cold density, so the field a test particle feels is not a functional of the
              metric and the scalar alone -- the force law reads the matter census.
          magnitude at f = 1: median kernel share of the total acceleration eta = 0.137 (L50 at f = 1 without suppression: 0.326).
          Neither is a laboratory or Solar-System effect: it takes a cold overdensity comparable to
          the local baryon density, and there is 3.8e-15 M_sun of cold matter inside Saturn's orbit
          against Pitjev-Pitjeva's 6.7e-11 (17603x margin). Baryons and photons stay
          minimally coupled to the single metric g, so gamma_PPN, Eotvos and MICROSCOPE are untouched.
  [FAIL] E1 the equivalence-principle cost is confined to the dark sector and is no worse in kind than L50's single between-sector violation   (it is confined to the dark sector EMPIRICALLY -- no laboratory or Solar-System test fires, margin 17603x on the Saturn bound -- but it is worse IN KIND. L50's violation is that two species fall differently. This lane adds a second, sharper one: the acceleration of a baryon depends on the abundance of a species it is not made of, so the gravitational field is not determined by the total stress-energy even in principle. Magnitude eta = 0.14. Priced as a structural cost, not an empirical one)

    E2  FREE FUNCTIONS AND PARAMETERS, counted against the deposited theory:
