==========================================================================================================================
PART V -- VERDICT, AND THE THEOREM.
==========================================================================================================================
  [FAIL] V1 [THE LANE'S QUESTION] the kernel can be suppressed where cold matter dominates in a way that lets the galaxy window reach f = 1 WHILE LEAVING THE GALAXY-SCALE MOND PHENOMENOLOGY INTACT   (NO, and the two halves separate cleanly. The mechanism IS outside L6's closed class (B1-B4), and it DOES open the three-way intersection (D2): on the local reading with s = f_b^4 the galaxy ceiling is 1.073 / 1.018, clusters need 1.055 +/- 0.125, the CMB fixes 1.000, and every gate the deposited theory passes still passes. But 'intact' fails: the kernel's share of the observed deep-MOND anomaly is capped at W <= 0.389 on both footings (D4), against 0.888 in the deposited theory, because the halo at the CMB's own abundance already supplies 109% of that anomaly. What survives is a kernel whose own MOND transition sits at a_0' <= 0.19 a_0 (D5), while the observed turnover, the BTFR zero point and the bounded-boost ceiling are all the halo's (D7) -- so the a_0-Lambda tie loses the galaxy measurement kappa is quoted from)
  [FAIL] V2 the pincer can be opened while the MOND sector still does MOST of the galaxy-scale dynamical work, on ANY function of ANY variable, environmental or compositional   (it cannot, and D4 shows this is a bound rather than a failed search: eleven functions on two readings of f_b all land on the single uniform-suppression curve at their own median deep-MOND strength, to within 0.122 in the ceiling and 0.056 in W. The galaxy data constrain exactly ONE number, and f = 1 on both footings forces it below 0.438, hence W <= 0.389)

    V3  THE THEOREM, stated generally because the programme deserves the statement rather than one
        more dead mechanism:
      The observed galaxy-scale anomaly is ONE number per point, g_obs - g_bar.  At the cold abundance the CMB fixes,
      the abundance-matched LambdaCDM halo alone already supplies 109% of it and reproduces SPARC at 0.171 dex with
      median -0.026.  Whatever the MOND kernel adds at that abundance is therefore an overshoot, and the galaxy window
      can be reached only by suppressing the kernel to an effective strength s_eff <= 0.438 where the anomaly is
      measured.  That bound is a statement about the DATA and the halo, not about the kernel's functional form: D4
      verifies that eleven suppression functions, keyed to two different composition variables, all reduce to the same
      one number as far as the galaxy data are concerned.  It is therefore invariant under every remaining move -- re-
      sourcing the scalar (L50), screening on an environmental scalar (L6), or keying the kernel to the species
      composition (this lane).  Each is only a different way of choosing s_eff.

      HENCE, quantitatively: at Omega_c h^2 = 0.1200 the kernel may supply at most W = 0.39 of the observed deep-MOND
      galaxy anomaly, against 0.89 in the theory without a cold component; and because a partial suppression is
      exactly degenerate with a smaller a_0 in the deep-MOND limit, the surviving term's own MOND transition sits at
      a_0' <= 0.19 a_0, a factor 5.2 below where the observed relation turns over, and the turnover, the BTFR zero
      point and the bounded-boost ceiling are all set by the halo instead.  A FULL COLD ABUNDANCE AND A MOND KERNEL
      DOING THE GALAXY WORK ARE ALTERNATIVES, NOT COMPLEMENTS -- not because the pincer stays shut, but because they
      are two explanations of the SAME measured excess and the excess can only be spent once.  The theory can have the
      CMB, the clusters and the growth of structure, at which point its kernel is at most a third-strength correction
      whose own MOND scale is five times too small, and none of its distinctive predictions survives as a test; or it
      can have the galaxy phenomenology at f = 0, at which point S_eff = 0 exactly and it fails the CMB and linear
      growth outright.

      What is NOT claimed.  Nothing here favours this framework over LambdaCDM and nothing here constrains LambdaCDM:
      the cold component, its abundance-matched profile and its stellar-to-halo-mass relation are LambdaCDM's,
      imported wholesale, and a per-galaxy NFW with two free parameters reaches 0.061 dex where the kernel reaches
      0.145 (L28 / L49 W1).  Nor is this a closure of MOND-like theories in general: it closes the combination of THIS
      action's kernel with a full cold abundance whose galaxy profile is LambdaCDM's.  A theory whose cold component
      is distributed differently -- less in galaxies, more elsewhere -- is not covered, though L49's specification and
      the 2026-09-06/07 dark-sector no-go between them close every mechanism so far proposed for making one.  And the
      opening exhibited in D2 is a real result that should not be talked away: the pincer that closed L49 and L50 does
      open, on a mechanism genuinely outside L6's class.  It is the price, not the arithmetic, that makes it not worth
      taking.

    CAVEATS, stated rather than buried:
      1. The GENEROUS of L49's two galaxy criteria (|median| < 0.11 dex) is carried throughout, so the
         candidate is not handed a manufactured deficit. D6 shows the strict criterion cannot be used
         here at all: at f = 1 the halo ALONE already misses it, independently of any kernel.
      2. The local-midplane f_b uses SBdisk/SBbul photometry for stars and a thin-disc inversion of
         V_gas for gas, at a fixed scale height. C4 varies h_z over 0.15-1.00 kpc and E2 shows the
         mechanism's key number s_eff swings by a large factor across that range -- so the local
         horn's success is h_z-controlled and is reported as such, not as a robust result.
      3. Abundance matching carries ~0.30 dex of systematic on log M200 (Moster vs Behroozi vs
         Kravtsov). It moves the galaxy ceiling and the cluster requirement together. It does not
         touch the theorem, which is about the halo ALREADY supplying the anomaly at f = 1.
      4. D9's fifth force on the cold component is an ORDER-OF-MAGNITUDE estimate from dln s/dln rho_c,
         not a solved profile. It is the mechanism's largest unpaid bill and it is flagged, not
         resolved: every halo number in this lane assumes dust, which under this action it is not.
      5. Cluster windows use the enclosed baryon fraction inside the same 1000 kpc aperture as L50, at
         b = 0 and b = 0.20. The hydrostatic bias is not resolved here.
      6. The kernel, its saturation constant and the closure locus are the deposited theory's,
         unchanged; nothing here re-fits them, and kappa remains FITTED (0.4998 / 0.6023).

